From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CVE-2026-21226: Replace pickle with JSON for continuation tokens

This patch addresses a critical security vulnerability (CVE-2026-21226) where
pickle.loads() was used to deserialize continuation tokens. Pickle
deserialization can execute arbitrary code when processing malicious input.

The fix replaces pickle serialization with JSON serialization for all
continuation token operations, using an allowlist approach for headers
to prevent sensitive data leakage.

Changes:
- New file: azure/core/polling/_utils.py - Shared utilities for safe JSON-based
  continuation token serialization
- Modified: azure/core/polling/_poller.py - Use JSON instead of pickle for
  _SansIONoPolling continuation tokens
- Modified: azure/core/polling/base_polling.py - Use JSON instead of pickle for
  _SansIOLROBasePolling continuation tokens, add minimal HTTP response class for
  token reconstruction

Security improvements:
- Continuation tokens are now JSON-serialized instead of pickle-serialized
- Old pickle-based tokens are detected and rejected with helpful error message
- Sensitive headers (Authorization, Cookie, etc.) are filtered from tokens
- Only LRO-related headers are preserved in continuation tokens

